From 8863b08a3becb7ecca3387e8f29bc3ea01fdc4c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SECURITY-D4: only the server writes in the notice banner

Success messages ride the redirect as ?notice=<text>, and any link could
put its own words in the app's own banner - escaped, so never a script,
but phishing with the app's authority ("your account is locked, call
..."). Messages are dynamic (names, amounts), so a fixed set of keys would
not do; instead withNotice signs each notice with an HMAC keyed by a
random per-process secret, and noticeFrom shows only a notice whose
signature matches its text. The kind parameter was never set by any
redirect and is no longer read. The CAS page's ?error=<text> becomes a
fixed key. Every existing message still arrives unchanged; a restart
between a redirect and its page drops that one notice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
